flowchart TB
    accTitle: Different observations, common working interface
    accDescr: Physical perception, dialogue replies, and digital results can follow different representation paths before information becomes available in working memory.

    subgraph INPUTS[External information]
      direction LR
      PHYS[Physical perception]
      DIAL[Dialogue reply]
      DIG[Digital result]
    end
    PHYS --> REP[Representation for the agent]
    DIAL --> REP
    DIG --> REP
    REP --> WM[Working memory]

    PHYS -.-> NOTE1[Image, audio, or tactile signal]
    DIAL -.-> NOTE2[Natural-language response]
    DIG -.-> NOTE3[Page, API response, or code result]

    classDef input fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.2px;
    classDef process fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef store fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.5px;
    class PHYS,DIAL,DIG,NOTE1,NOTE2,NOTE3 input;
    class REP process;
    class WM store;
